   "id": "bava_metzia.28b.21",
   "daf": "28b",
   "sentenceId": 20,
   "he": "וְשֶׁאֵינוֹ עוֹשֶׂה וְאוֹכֵל. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: ״וַהֲשֵׁבוֹתוֹ לוֹ״ – רְאֵה הֵיאַךְ תְּשִׁיבֶנּוּ לוֹ, שֶׁלֹּא יַאֲכִיל עֵגֶל לַעֲגָלִים, וּסְיָח לִסְיָיחִין, אֲווֹזָא לַאֲווֹזִין, וְתַרְנְגוֹל לְתַרְנְגוֹלִין.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «And» any living being «that does not work but» it does «eat» shall be sold. «The Sages taught» in a baraita: The verse states: «“And you shall return it to him”» (Deuteronomy 22:2), indicating that the finder must «see how» best «to return it to him,» meaning «that» one «shall not feed» the value of «a calf to» the lost «calves» that he is tending, «nor» the value of «a foal to» the lost «foals» that he is tending, «nor» the value of «a goose to» the «geese» that he is tending, «nor» the value of «a rooster to» the «roosters» that he is tending. Were the finder to do so, ultimately, the owner would receive nothing."
  }
 ],
